# Multimodal Stress Detection — Implementation Plan

Train deep learning models on the **WorkStress3D dataset** to detect stress by fusing physiological signals, facial expressions, and survey data. Trained models will later be used for real-time inference with a wearable glove.

---

## 1. Dataset Summary

### Physiological Signals (20 subjects)

| File | Samples | Features |
|------|---------|----------|
| `physiological_signals_15sn.csv` | 39,200 | Subject, eda, bvp, temp, x, y, z, emotion |
| `physiological_signals_30sn.csv` | 82,600 | Same (column name: `subjet`) |
| `physiological_signals_60sn.csv` | 168,000 | Same |

**Labels**: 0 = Calm (65%), 1 = Stress (34%), 2 = Amusement (0.6%)

### Facial Expressions

| File | Samples | Format |
|------|---------|--------|
| `facial_expression.csv` | 83 | emotion (0=non-stress, 1=stress), pixels (48×48) |

### Survey Data (enrichment features)

| File | Records | Role in Model |
|------|---------|---------------|
| `generalStressTest.csv` | 20 | Baseline stress score per subject → appended as feature |
| `PANAS.csv` | 20 | 10 affect scores per subject → appended as features |
| `instantQuestionnaires.csv` | 651 | Self-reported mood → label validation + context features |
| `demographic.csv` | 20 | Age, gender, etc. → encoded subject-level features |

